            "prompt": "red?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{53}{100}$",
              "worked": "$$P(\\text{red})\\approx\\frac{53}{100}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q4-a-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "not green?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{23}{25}$",
              "worked": "$100-8=92$ draws were not green.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{not green})&\\approx\\frac{92}{100}\\\\P(\\text{not green})&\\approx\\frac{23}{25}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 21
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If the bag contains 10 counters, how many counters of each colour do you think are in the bag?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Approximately 2 blue, 2 yellow, 5 red and 1 green.\n\nMultiply each observed relative frequency by 10 and round to a whole counter.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Blue counters}&\\approx10\\times\\frac{18}{100}=1.8\\approx2\\\\\\text{Yellow counters}&\\approx10\\times\\frac{21}{100}=2.1\\approx2\\\\\\text{Red counters}&\\approx10\\times\\frac{53}{100}=5.3\\approx5\\\\\\text{Green counters}&\\approx10\\times\\frac{8}{100}=0.8\\approx1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThese estimates total $2+2+5+1=10$ counters.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
